  "primaryAnswer": "A",
  "alternativeAnswers": [],
  "acceptanceMode": "exact",
  "hint": "Secant is $\\frac{1}{\\cos x}$, and $\\cos x$ lives between $-1$ and $1$.",
  "hints": [
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "text": "Secant is $\\frac{1}{\\cos x}$, and $\\cos x$ lives between $-1$ and $1$."
    },
    {
      "level": "guide",
      "text": "Dividing $1$ by something small makes something BIG. What is the smallest that $|\\sec x|$ can be?"
    },
    {
      "level": "reveal",
      "text": "The best case is $\\cos x = \\pm 1$, giving $\\sec x = \\pm 1$; every other value is further from zero."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": [
    "Since $|\\cos x| \\le 1$, taking the reciprocal gives $|\\sec x| \\ge 1$.",
    "So secant can equal $1$ or $-1$ but nothing in between.",
    "The range is $y \\le -1$ or $y \\ge 1$ — the graph is made of U-shaped branches that never enter the strip between the lines $y = 1$ and $y = -1$."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Try a few numbers",
      "steps": [
        "$\\cos x = 1 \\Rightarrow \\sec x = 1$. $\\cos x = 0.5 \\Rightarrow \\sec x = 2$. $\\cos x = 0.1 \\Rightarrow \\sec x = 10$.",
        "As cosine shrinks toward $0$, secant races off to infinity.",
        "There is no value of $x$ that makes $\\sec x$ equal, say, $0.4$ — nothing lands inside the gap."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    "secant",
    "range",
